  (W, "A finite field of prime order p, written F_p, is the set of whole numbers from 0 to p minus 1 together with the four arithmetic operations, in which every result is replaced by its remainder after division by p. The book writes the remainder operation as 'mod p' and says that it indicates that the curve is over a finite field of prime order p [BK]. Because the remainder always lies between 0 and p minus 1, the numbers never grow beyond the size of p, and every non-zero number has a partner by which it can be multiplied to give 1."),
