  (Y, "Bitcoin leans on SHA256 for many jobs. This chapter meets it as the first step of HASH160, as the double hash that gives base58check its checksum and as the function the book recommends for turning random bits into a private key candidate. Using one well-studied function in all these places keeps the system simple, and it means that a weakness in it would affect everything at once."),
